course: dictionary
lesson: 2635
title: Destiny: what is meant to happen
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Destiny means what will happen to someone in the future, especially when it seems already decided, as if fate or a higher power has planned it. «It was her destiny to be a doctor» means she was meant to become a doctor.
explain: Destiny can also mean a power, called fate, that some people believe controls the future. Stories often ask whether people can choose their own destiny, or whether it is already fixed.
explain: Watch for capital letters. In «Destiny shares a room with a girl called Precious», Destiny is a girl's name, not the word. Ask yourself: does the sentence make sense if I swap in fate or future? If not, it may be a name.
fact: Destiny is a noun, and its plural is destinies.
fact: «Destiny» means what will happen to someone in the future, especially when it seems already decided.
fact: «Destiny» can mean the important job or role someone seems meant to have, as in «It was her destiny to be a doctor».
fact: «Destiny» is another word for fate, the power some people believe controls the future.
fact: A capital D can mean a name, as in «Destiny shares a room with a girl called Precious».
exercise: «It was her destiny to be a doctor.» What does destiny mean here? | *What her future was meant to be | A hospital where she works | A new car she wanted | A holiday she planned
exercise: In «Destiny shares a room with a girl called Precious», what is Destiny? | A kind of room | A type of hoodie | A place to sleep | *A girl's name
exercise: Which phrase means you are in charge of what happens to you? | it was his destiny | meet your destiny | *control your own destiny | a sense of destiny
test: What is a destiny? | A school subject | *What will happen to someone in the future | A kind of weather | A type of sport
test: Another word for destiny, meaning the power that controls the future, is what? | Holiday | *Fate | Kindness | Freedom
exam: Which sentence uses destiny to mean the future that seems already decided? | We walked to the park after school. | *It was his destiny to lead the kingdom. | She ate a sandwich at lunch. | Destiny shares a room with a girl called Precious.
